{
  "query": "A travel booking startup at scrumtuous.com plans to move a self-managed MySQL workload from its own data center into Google Cloud. They require minimal downtime during cutover, the ability to continue applying schema changes while the migration runs, built-in data validation with the option to roll back if problems occur, and a target that is a globally distributed and highly scalable managed relational database. Which pairing of a Google Cloud migration tool and a managed database service should they select?",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Database Migration Service and Cloud Bigtable",
      "explanation": "This combines Google Cloud&apos;s managed migration tool with a wide column NoSQL service designed for massive scale and low latency.",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Database Migration Service and Cloud Spanner",
      "explanation": "This uses Google Cloud&apos;s native migration service in conjunction with a globally distributed and strongly consistent relational database.",
      "correct": true,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Cloud Dataflow and Firestore",
      "explanation": "This pairs a stream and batch processing service with a document database that is designed for flexible schemas and high availability.",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Database Migration Service and Cloud SQL for MySQL",
      "explanation": "This leverages Google Cloud&apos;s managed migration service to move MySQL into a fully managed regional MySQL offering.",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    }
  ],
  "answer": "<p>The correct option is <b>Database Migration Service and Cloud Spanner</b>. This pairing satisfies the need for minimal downtime during cutover, supports ongoing schema changes while replication runs, provides built-in validation with a safe cutover and rollback path, and delivers a globally distributed and highly scalable managed relational database.</p><p><b>Database Migration Service</b> supports continuous replication from MySQL which enables near zero downtime cutovers. It includes connectivity checks, migration validation, and controlled promotion so you can verify the target before redirecting traffic which gives you a clear rollback path by keeping the source as the system of record until cutover is confirmed.</p><p><b>Cloud Spanner</b> is a fully managed relational database that is globally distributed with strong consistency and automatic scaling. It is designed for high throughput and low latency across regions which matches the requirement for a globally distributed and highly scalable managed relational target.</p><p><i>Database Migration Service and Cloud Bigtable</i> is not suitable because Cloud Bigtable is a wide column NoSQL database rather than a relational database, so it does not align with a MySQL relational workload or SQL semantics.</p><p><i>Cloud Dataflow and Firestore</i> is incorrect because Cloud Dataflow is a general data processing service rather than a purpose built database migration tool with native CDC and validation, and Firestore is a document oriented NoSQL database rather than a relational target.</p><p><i>Database Migration Service and Cloud SQL for MySQL</i> does not meet the requirement for a globally distributed and massively scalable database. Cloud SQL is a managed relational service but it is regional and does not provide the global distribution and horizontal scalability characteristics that are central to this scenario.</p>",
